ore_value = evaluate_fitness(candidate_result)[0]\n        \n        if score_value < best_score:\n            best_sequence = candidate_result.copy()\n            best_score = score_value\n            \n        # Extend to larger lengths if time permits\n        if time.time() - start_time < budget_s - 60:\n            candidate_length = 1024\n            initial_seq = get_template_sequence(candidate_length, template_type='linear')\n            result_polish = polish_sequence(initial_seq, candidate_length, time_budget=40, checkpoint=True)\n            # Combine and check global best\n    except np.inf:  # Fallback to secondary profiles if invalid\n        initial_seq = get_template_sequence(candidate_length=512, template_type='linear')\n        candidate_result = main_search_function(initial_seq)\n        best_score = evaluate_fitness(candidate_result)\n    \n    # Final selection of optimal sequence across all lengths\n    if best_score < final_optimal_score(2048):\n        final_sequence = best_sequence.copy()\n    else:\n        with np.errstate(divide='ignore'):\n            final_sequence = log_norm(best_sequence, time_decay_factor, len(best_sequence), max_inc)\n    \n    return final_sequence.tolist()\n```\n\n**4. Search Choices and Useful Variations**  \n- **Initial Templates**: Start with periodic sequences (linear, cosine, sine_sq) based on research from seismoacoustic processing.  \n- **Mutation Factor**: Initialize dynamically for each candidate length (e.g., 0.8 for smaller sequences).  \n- **Descent Fraction**: Use \\( t = 0.7 \\) for each step, adapting upon stagnation.  \n- **Fallback Mechanism**: Random sequences are paired with elite results from other lengths for broadening exploration.  \n\n**5. Compute Budget and Robustness**  \n- **Population Size**: 20-50 for each initial trial (reduced from previous).  \n- **Local Optimization Iterations**: 400 seconds allocated for polishing at each length (initially 512).  \n- **Extended Runtime**: Up to 5 doublings (e.g., 512, 1024, 2048) if \\( 0.01 \\) norm is achieved.  \n- **Clamp Handling**: Automatically adjust sequences using logarithmic normalization to stay between \\( 0 \\) and \\( 1000 \\).  \n\n**6. Validation and Return Contract**  \n- **Exact Feasibility Check**: Use `evaluate_sequence` on all potential results to validate.  \n- **History Tracking**: Compute gradients across iterations to guide future steps (momentum-based).  \n- **Final Output**: A sequence (as a Python list) with non-negative entries and sum \u2265 0.01.",
